  "88": ["Where to stop and park", "Stop and park on the right side of the road, on the roadside, or at the carriageway edge if there is no roadside. In settlements on one way roads, or roads with one lane each way and no tram, the left side is allowed too.", "On which side of a two way road may you normally park?", ["The right side", "The left side", "In the middle"]],
  "89": ["How to park", "Park in one row, parallel to the carriageway edge. Two wheelers without sidecars may park in two rows if they hinder nobody. Parking at a sidewalk edge only where sign 5.15 with an extra sign allows.", "How must cars normally be parked on the carriageway?", ["In one row, parallel to the edge", "Nose in at an angle", "In two rows"]],
  "91": ["Stopping prohibited: tracks, tunnels, bridges", "Stopping is prohibited on tram tracks, at railway crossings, in tunnels, on bridges and overpasses with fewer than three lanes per direction, and under them unless signed.", "Where is stopping prohibited?", ["At a railway crossing", "On a wide parking area", "At a kerb with a free lane"]],
  "91b": ["Stopping prohibited: crossings", "Stopping is prohibited on pedestrian crossings and within 10 m before them, and on cycle path crossings and within 10 m before them.", "How close before a pedestrian crossing may you stop?", ["Not within 10 m", "Right up to it", "Not within 1 m"]],
  "91c": ["Stopping prohibited: junctions", "Stopping is prohibited at junctions of carriageways and within 30 m of the edge of the crossing carriageway, except the far side of a T junction separated by a solid line or median.", "How far from the edge of a crossing carriageway is stopping prohibited?", ["Within 30 m", "Within 5 m", "Within 100 m"]],
  "91d": ["Stopping prohibited: stops", "Stopping is prohibited at stops of route vehicles and within 15 m before or after the stop, except briefly boarding or dropping off if you do not hinder buses.", "How close to a bus stop is stopping prohibited?", ["Within 15 m", "Within 2 m", "Within 50 m"]],
  "91e": ["Stopping prohibited: visibility and gap", "Stopping is also prohibited where the gap to a continuous line, median or opposite edge is under 3 m, near crests and dangerous bends with visibility under 100 m, and where you block signals, signs, exits or pedestrians.", "Stopping is prohibited where visibility is under…", ["100 m", "300 m", "10 m"]],
  "92": ["Parking prohibited", "Parking is prohibited wherever stopping is prohibited, within 50 m of a railway crossing on either side, and under signs 3.27 to 3.30 or lines 1.4 and 1.10. Trucks may not be left at the roadside at night in a way that endangers others.", "How close to a railway crossing is parking prohibited?", ["Within 50 m", "Within 5 m", "Within 500 m"]],
  "93": ["Forced stop in a prohibited place", "If you must stop in a place where stopping is prohibited, take every measure to move the vehicle to the roadside and away from that place.", "You broke down in a no stopping zone. What must you do?", ["Do everything to move off the road and away", "Leave it there", "Switch off the lights and wait"]],
