  // Junctions in general
  "96": ["Turning: give way to pedestrians", "A driver turning left or right gives way to pedestrians crossing the road being entered, and to cyclists and personal mobility riders crossing from a cycle path.", "Turning right at a junction, whom do you give way to?", ["Pedestrians crossing the road you enter", "Nobody", "Only cars"]],
  "97": ["Do not block the junction", "If a jam would force you to stop and block cross traffic, do not enter the junction. If you have passed the stop line, do not enter the crossing of carriageways.", "A jam ahead of the junction. What do you do?", ["Do not enter if you would block cross traffic", "Enter and wait in the middle", "Honk"]],
  "98": ["Regulated and unregulated junctions", "A junction is regulated if lights or a controller set the order. With flashing yellow, broken lights or no controller it is unregulated. In a roundabout, vehicles already in it have priority.", "In a roundabout, who has priority?", ["Vehicles already in the roundabout", "Vehicles entering", "The bigger vehicle"]],
  "99": ["Turning left on green", "On a permitting signal, a driver turning left or making a U turn gives way to oncoming vehicles going straight and turning right. Tram drivers follow the same rule.", "On green you turn left. Whom do you give way to?", ["Oncoming vehicles going straight or turning right", "Nobody", "Vehicles behind you"]],
  "100": ["Green arrow section", "A driver moving on a green arrow of an additional section while red or yellow is on gives way to vehicles coming from other directions.", "You go on the green arrow while the main light is red. Whom do you give way to?", ["Vehicles from other directions", "Nobody", "Only pedestrians"]],
  "101": ["Trams at regulated junctions", "If the signals let a tram and other vehicles move at once, the tram goes first whatever the direction.", "A tram and a car both have green. Who goes first?", ["The tram", "The car", "The faster one"]],
  "102": ["Leaving a junction on green", "A driver who entered on a permitting signal keeps going in the intended direction whatever the lights, unless there are stop lines or signs at lights inside the junction, which must be obeyed.", "You entered on green and the light changed. What do you do?", ["Continue in your direction, unless stop lines inside require otherwise", "Stop in the middle", "Reverse"]],
  "103": ["Green is not a free pass", "On green, give way to vehicles finishing their passage through the junction and to pedestrians still crossing in the proper direction.", "Green light, but a pedestrian is still crossing. What do you do?", ["Let the pedestrian finish", "Drive on", "Honk"]],

